    "$aircraftComment":  "Curated, because MSFS 2024 packages are opaque .fsarchive blobs and the four facts cannot be read from disk (verified 2026-09-03). \u0027icao\u0027 is the ICAO type code (B350, DA62) - what SimBrief reports and what the app records, so it is the key the preflight gate looks an aircraft up by. \u0027match\u0027 is the FSUIPC profile name ([Profile.\u003cmatch\u003e] / [Axes.\u003cmatch\u003e]). \u0027titleMatch\u0027 is the substring FSUIPC matches the sim\u0027s aircraft TITLE on - it must come from the title FSUIPC actually logs (Aircraft=\"...\" in FSUIPC7.log), never from a package name: the 350\u0027s package is kingair350 but its title is \"Beechcraft King Air\", and guessing cost a flight with dead levers. When titleMatch is absent, match is used for both. \u0027facts\u0027 are what the classification rule needs; \u0027layout\u0027 is what they resolve to. \u0027verified\u0027 says how the entry is known: flown means the levers were seen driving the right controls in the sim; type means it follows from the aircraft type and has not been flown yet. Add an aircraft only with both facts answered - never guess them.",
